msgid "Common Power Module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:11
#: e2e593a7f7e34171a026eb60c8c1bbd6
msgid "Many autopilots can be purchased with an analog power module that provides a stable power supply to the autopilot and also supports measuring the battery voltage and current consumption."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:14
#: 5ec2eddc903d4fedaacebe6f8acbf8e2
msgid "Specifications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:16
#: 9c909e110b894b15b88d471ce83d77aa
msgid "Below are typical limits, but it is best to confirm directly with the vendor:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:18
#: 1c4bd9c13aab40918573115734768c3c
msgid "Maximum input voltage of 18V (4S lipo)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:19
#: 5e55a786d9a74c83b16e1e4d189476f5
msgid "Maximum of 90 Amps (but only capable of measuring up to 60 Amps)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:20
#: 139f9abd6346415b9480b44453228cc9
msgid "Provides 5.37V and 2.25Amp power supply to the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:24
#: 0d6bb42f68114c66bc0d5a557ea0f981
msgid "The Power Module provides enough power for the autopilot, receiver, and a few low powered peripherals (lidar, telemetry) but does not have enough power for servos or high current devices like FPV transmitters or the RFD900 radios.  More information on :ref:`powering the Pixhawk can be found here <common-powering-the-pixhawk>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:26
#: 07ed84cde5914396a1023ac42cec2bca
msgid "Power Modules of this type (resistive shunt) cannot continuously support their maximum rated current. Excessive and destructive heat can be generated at continuous current levels exceeding 33% to 66% of the maximum rated current (instantaneous rating). Check with manufacturer for ratings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:29
#: aec4042b9e004295bb4b290487dda0bf
msgid "Connecting to the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:31
#: 53f1b444775a43b5abd82bd37e93cb23
msgid "The 6 pin cable from the power module plugs into the POWER port of the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:37
#: f2237fa6f33f41fdbb55b7bf20391f6d
msgid "The battery is connected to the power module's male connector.  The ESC or Power Distribution Board should be connected to the power module's female connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:40
#: 0e160a489440408684562c042c2c9265
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:42
#: 6e6fa17ffefa45f684878997920d2163
msgid "Most ground stations provide a battery monitor interface but the parameters can also be set manually:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:44
#: cfe79eb3ac484aa29475fb914a730861
msgid ":ref:`BATT_MONITOR <BATT_MONITOR>` = **3** to measure only voltage or **4** to measure both voltage and current (you will need to reboot the board after changing this)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:45
#: 62d617121e9e4ce4b4f1d2eb1861bfb5
msgid ":ref:`BATT_VOLT_PIN<BATT_VOLT_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = **2**. The autopilot pin connected to the power module's voltage pin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:46
#: ecc1fe08507d40a4b34f837dfa4f521f
msgid ":ref:`BATT_VOLT_MULT<BATT_VOLT_MULT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` converts the analog voltage received from the power module's voltage pin to the battery's voltage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:47
#: c5f4f981cec54d1394c38dcdfa172826
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CURR_PIN<BATT_CURR_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = **3**. The autopilot pin connected to the power module's current pin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:48
#: 2102072225ce4177b00553ec385f8bf0
msgid ":ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` converts the analog voltage received from the power module's current pin to the battery's current"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:49
#: 1b606daad1bf40eda5b1ec5e08096025
msgid ":ref:`BATT_AMP_OFFSET <BATT_AMP_OFFSET__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` voltage offset received from the power module's current pin when there is no current being pulled from the battery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:51
#: 366c7d2dd4a944b58f4585a05746059f
msgid "Instructions for setup and calibration using the :ref:`Mission Planner can be found here <common-power-module-configuration-in-mission-planner>` A Blog post with instructions for `set-up using QGC can be found here <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/t/power-monitor-setup-on-ardupilot-copter-3-6/35441>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:55
#: 4c81578079a84ed7ba0ff1268963da86
msgid "Dual Battery Monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:57
#: c46cc7e172a6427383dcac9715994f8d
msgid "If the autopilot has additional analog-to-digital pins available, a second battery can be monitored by setting up the ``BATT2_`` parameters.  The values below allow reading a second battery's voltage and current using :ref:`The Cube's <common-thecube-overview>` POWER2 port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:59
#: 48e4018e88434b178d3c2f6b7933eb07
msgid ":ref:`BATT2_MONITOR <BATT2_MONITOR>` = **4** to measure both voltage and current (you will need to reboot the board after changing this)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:60
#: 291e3a75c34340819929b8c9db990734
msgid ":ref:`BATT2_VOLT_PIN <BATT2_VOLT_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = **13**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:61
#: 22a885e8324b433696fb3a463c67dfd3
msgid ":ref:`BATT2_CURR_PIN <BATT2_CURR_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = **14**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:63
#: 80b8f7f858a041a8bd57d8e3d19254e5
msgid "The :ref:`BATT2_VOLT_MULT <BATT2_VOLT_MULT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` and :ref:`BATT2_AMP_PERVLT <BATT2_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` should also be set by comparing the reported values vs values collected using a hand held voltage meter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:70
#: 44334c7c9bb64e11a909d664a5e1ab5b
msgid "Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:74
#: a1b14cee87904cf697efa1ade1994a05
msgid "Instructions for :ref:`battery failsafe can be found here <apms-failsafe-function>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:79
#: c718090733b742d681fb7fb953ce0295
msgid "Extending Current Measurement Capacity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:81
#: efb56380054c43a8a3812017d1d9b80a
msgid "Shunt resistor power monitors of this variety can be used to measure higher currents if setup in a current sharing configuration, as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:86
#: 349c0976592a4cd1936963565b881799
msgid "Design points:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:88
#: 150fedeffbba433eac2ae84954318813
msgid "The shunt should be approximately the same resistance as the power module. For example, a 120A module usually uses a 0.5 milliohm sense resistor. Therefore the wire shunt should be ~ 0.5 milliohm for equal sharing of the total current. This can be determined from a reference such as `this <https://www.engineeringtoolbox.com/wire-gauges-d_419.html>`_ . For 12ga wire, that would be ~ 4 inches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:89
#: 3c7ae02eaf854ff886efa0d7937c091e
msgid "The wire gauge (and, of course, the wire used to connect the power module) should be rated to handle the expected continuous current for the length of wiring utilized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:90
#: cf7e0b573a1645eb88e4abcfb54c3838
msgid "Try to keep the leads from the shunt junctions to power module short. Longer leads to the module there will increase resistance in that branch. This will unbalance the current split. Not an large issue, but will effectively increase the max resistance capability and decrease the incremental sensitivity of the measurement more than needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:96
#: 5432f2e10dc744698917fb0592b13a8d
msgid "In the photo above, by providing two bypasses, the current is shared such that the power monitor sees a little less than 1/3 the total current flowing, and reports a value ~1/3 normal, extending its range ~3X."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:98
#: e092191a184647e1b247df2666bf81b4
msgid "Due to variations in materials, length, etc. it is mandatory that the monitor be calibrated using a precision current meter of some kind. It is best to calibrate at a value greater than 50% of the maximum current expected."
msgstr ""
